<title>USA: Mylan gets OK to market hypertension drug.</title>
<headline>Mylan gets OK to market hypertension drug.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mylan Laboratories Inc said Tuesday it has received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to manufacture and market Guanfacine Hydrochloride tablets in 1 mg and 2 mg strengths.</p>
<p>Guanfacine is the generic equivalent of Tenex, an A.H. Robins Co product used to manage hypertension.</p>
<p>Mylan said it plans to begin shipping the Guanfacine immediately.</p>
</text>
